{
 "id": "lem-trf-etale-relation-finding-opens",
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Restriction of a quotient by an fppf relation is an open subspace",
 "statement": "Let $S$ be a scheme [def-pc-scheme], let $U$ be a scheme over $S$, and let $(s,t):R\\to U\\times_SU$ [def-pc-fibre-product] be an equivalence relation whose two projections $s,t:R\\to U$ are surjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation. Let $g:U'\\to U$ be flat and locally of finite presentation, and let $R'$ be the restriction of $R$ to $U'$. On the big fppf site $(\\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ [def-pc-fppf-site], write $F=U/R$ and $F'=U'/R'$ for the sheafified quotient presheaves [def-weil-pbc-sheafification]. Then the natural map $F'\\to F$ is representable and an open immersion.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/stacks-project/spaces.tex",
  "place": "Tag 02WU (finding-opens), using Tag 02VH for restriction of the relation and Tags 023Q/02W2 for fppf descent of opens"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-pc-scheme",
  "def-pc-fibre-product",
  "def-pc-fppf-site",
  "def-weil-pbc-sheafification"
 ],
